Package: baatsun
Version: __VERSION__
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, ydotool, pipewire-bin | pipewire
Recommends: gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, gir1.2-gtk4layershell-1.0
Maintainer: Umar Bashir Rather <mail.umarbashir@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/umarbashirr/baatsun
Description: Offline push-to-talk voice dictation daemon
 Baatsun is a voice dictation tool for Linux: hold Ctrl+Super anywhere,
 speak, release, and the transcribed text (via faster-whisper, fully
 offline) is typed into whatever window has focus, via ydotool. Reads
 the keyboard directly below the compositor, so no shortcut needs to be
 registered anywhere and it works the same way on any desktop
 environment. Includes an always-on-top pill showing recording state
 (a GNOME Shell extension on GNOME, a layer-shell overlay elsewhere), a
 tray icon, and a searchable history window for browsing, copying, and
 retyping past transcripts.
